```

Note main uses flex-1 — Layout wraps Outlet in a flex-col min-h-screen div, so main flex-1 fills. Good.

max-h-[calc(100dvh-8rem)] on the aspect box: mobile — box aspect 9/16 with w full (e.g., 390px → 693px). 100dvh-8rem ≈ viewport-128px; on iPhone 14 (844px) → 716px > 693 → no clamp. On shorter phones (667px viewport → 539px) → clamp kicks in, element box shorter, video letterboxes inside (object-contain) — acceptable, no crop.

grid-cols-6 for episodes in sidebar with only 4 episodes — fine, wraps.

One more consideration: aspect-[9/16] + max-h + w-full — with max-h binding, height = max-h, width stays full → box aspect not 9:16 anymore but object-contain keeps video correct. The plan gate: "视频始终 9:16" — the VIDEO stays 9:16 (object-contain), box may be taller ratio only when clamped (box wider than 9:16 → pillarbox? no: box w=400,h=clamped smaller → box becomes WIDER than 9:16 → video letterboxes with black on left/right? object-contain video 9:16 in wider box → video height = box height, width = height*9/16 < box width → pillarbox bars left/right, black on black bg, invisible. Fine, no crop/stretch.

